  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education: Schools Connect UK</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Schools Connect UK is one of the Global Programmes through which the British Council delivers its grant-funded activity. The primary focus of this Global Programme&#x2019;s ODA eligible activity and outcomes is described below. Schools Connect UK enhances the quality of primary and secondary education through international school partnerships.What we do:&#x25FC; Design and deliver international school partnerships.&#x25FC; Develop and disseminate research and evaluation.&#x25FC; Design and/or support professional development programmes / opportunities for practitioners. Why we do it:&#x25FC; To enhance the quality of primary and secondary education through international connections, partnerships and learning. &#x25FC; Support young people to be able to communicate internationally and respond to global challenges &#x25FC; Build mutually beneficial relationships between the UK and countries worldwide to build trust, enhance education policy and develop international perspectives.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x25FC; Contributing to raising the quality of education through international school partnerships.&#x25FC; Teachers have greater awareness of the importance of bringing international perspectives into the classroom.&#x25FC;Young people improve their ability to communicate and collaborate with international peers and their understanding of global challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x25FC;School teachers and leaders.&#x25FC; Young people.</narrative>
  </description>
